Skip Bukkit conversions in the per-equipment-change path when no event will read them.

LivingEntity#collectEquipmentChanges converts both the previous and current ItemStack to Bukkit
types on every changed slot. Those two asBukkitCopy calls are deep copies, and their only consumers
are EntityEquipmentChangedEvent and PlayerArmorChangeEvent. Both events were constructed and fired
unconditionally, so a server with no listener for either paid, per changed slot, for two ItemStack
copies, an EnumMap and an event object - all immediately discarded.

Leaf's Lithium equipment tracking already short-circuits this method when nothing changed, so this
targets the remaining case: equipment that genuinely did change on a server nobody is listening on.
Armoured mobs, armour stands and any mob that picks up items hit it.

Listener presence is resolved once per call rather than per slot. Semantics are unchanged: when a
listener exists, the copies are made and both events fire exactly as before.

--- a/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity.java
+++ b/leaf-server/src/minecraft/java/net/minecraft/world/entity/LivingEntity.java
@@ -3730,6 +3730,13 @@
+        // AtlasSpigot start - skip Bukkit conversions nothing is listening for
+        final boolean equipmentChangedListened = io.papermc.paper.event.entity.EntityEquipmentChangedEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length > 0;
+        final boolean armorChangeListened = com.destroystokyo.paper.event.player.PlayerArmorChangeEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length > 0;
+        // AtlasSpigot end
         for (EquipmentSlot slot : EquipmentSlot.VALUES_ARRAY) { // Gale - JettPack - reduce array allocations

@@ -3736,10 +3743,17 @@
-                final org.bukkit.inventory.ItemStack oldItem = CraftItemStack.asBukkitCopy(previous);
-                final org.bukkit.inventory.ItemStack newItem = CraftItemStack.asBukkitCopy(current);
-                if (this instanceof ServerPlayer && slot.getType() == EquipmentSlot.Type.HUMANOID_ARMOR) {
+                // AtlasSpigot start - only convert to Bukkit types when an event will actually read them
+                final boolean armorChangeWanted = armorChangeListened && this instanceof ServerPlayer && slot.getType() == EquipmentSlot.Type.HUMANOID_ARMOR;
+                org.bukkit.inventory.ItemStack oldItem = null;
+                org.bukkit.inventory.ItemStack newItem = null;
+                if (equipmentChangedListened || armorChangeWanted) {
+                    oldItem = CraftItemStack.asBukkitCopy(previous);
+                    newItem = CraftItemStack.asBukkitCopy(current);
+                }
+                if (armorChangeWanted) {
                     new com.destroystokyo.paper.event.player.PlayerArmorChangeEvent(...).callEvent();
                 }
+                // AtlasSpigot end

                 if (changedItems == null) {
                     changedItems = Maps.newEnumMap(EquipmentSlot.class);
-                    equipmentChanges = Maps.newEnumMap(org.bukkit.inventory.EquipmentSlot.class);
+                    if (equipmentChangedListened) equipmentChanges = Maps.newEnumMap(org.bukkit.inventory.EquipmentSlot.class); // AtlasSpigot - only when listened for
                 }

                 changedItems.put(slot, current);
-                equipmentChanges.put(CraftEquipmentSlot.getSlot(slot), new EquipmentChangeImpl(oldItem, newItem));
+                if (equipmentChangedListened) equipmentChanges.put(org.bukkit.craftbukkit.CraftEquipmentSlot.getSlot(slot), new EquipmentChangeImpl(oldItem, newItem)); // AtlasSpigot - only when listened for

@@ -3790,1 +3804,1 @@
-            new io.papermc.paper.event.entity.EntityEquipmentChangedEvent(this.getBukkitLivingEntity(), equipmentChanges).callEvent();
+            if (equipmentChangedListened) new io.papermc.paper.event.entity.EntityEquipmentChangedEvent(this.getBukkitLivingEntity(), equipmentChanges).callEvent(); // AtlasSpigot - skip when unlistened
